  "description": "Landscaping within rear yard to create 2no. petanque pistes.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Light from the luminaires shall not exceed 10 EV (lux) within suburban surroundings (or 25 EV (lux) within urban surroundings) when measured at any residential or light sensitive window overlooking the development.&nbsp; All luminaries shall be oriented and designed in such a way to minimise light spillage beyond the boundary and prevent glare into the windows of residential or light sensitive properties overlooking the development. The applicant must submit light contour maps to show how the proposed lighting scheme will impact on the surrounding residents. This scheme shall be submitted to the Local Authority Planners for approval before the lights are installed.&nbsp;Reason: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers and the surrounding area from light pollution",
    "&lt;p&gt;The Petanque courts may only be used between the hours of 10:00 and 22:00 on Monday -Sundays. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: In the interest of the amenities of adjoining occupiers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the commencement of the use hereby approved, an Event Management &amp;amp; Operating Plan shall be submitted to and approved by the local planning authority in writing. The plan shall set out full details of how the development will be operated and how customers will be managed leaving the premises at closing time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
